 "tips": {
  "wide": "Pick a seat over the wing, roughly the front of the main economy cabin just behind the over-wing exits. Avoid the last 10 rows.",
  "narrow": "Pick a seat over the wing, usually near the over-wing exit rows, roughly a third of the way back in economy. The last rows feel bumps the most.",
  "regional": "Sit over or just ahead of the wing. On rear-engine jets (CRJ), the rows around the wing are smoother but louder near the back.",
  "turboprop": "Sit in the middle rows under the wing. Turboprops fly lower and feel more bumps; the rows right at the propellers are the loudest."
